# Kept out of the build context for both web images.

# Installed inside the image by `npm ci`. A host tree copied in would be built
# for the host's platform and libc, which on macOS means native binaries that
# cannot run in an Alpine container — and it is the largest thing in this
# directory by far, so sending it also makes every build slower.
node_modules/

# The previous local `npm run build`. The production image builds its own; a
# stale one copied in would be silently served instead.
dist/
build/

# Local overrides, and never in an image: Vite inlines VITE_* values into the
# bundle at build time, so a developer's .env.local leaking into a production
# build bakes their machine's URLs into it.
.env
.env.local
.env.*.local

# Build state and noise.
*.tsbuildinfo
.vite/
*.log
npm-debug.log*
.DS_Store
